.y bu is not "u". .u bu is. And the u in ui is not pronounced [u] but [w] w=
hich *is* a consonant. Some here seem to lack reading comprehension. It's a=
nnoying to argue with people who won't listen to what the other person is s=
aying.
Whether or not something is a vowel depends on the way it's pronounced, not=
 the way it's written.

mu'o

